# `filter` from other languages: DS0104 pointing at `where`, with a fix.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | filter amount > 10
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..39
  PIPELINE@0..38
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..38
      IDENT@20..26 "filter"
      WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
      BIN_EXPR@27..38
        NAME_REF@27..33
          IDENT@27..33 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
        GT@34..35 ">"
        WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
        LITERAL@36..38
          LONG@36..38 "10"
  WHITESPACE@38..39 "\n"

error[DS0104]: unknown operator `filter`
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | filter amount > 10
  |                     ^^^^^^ not a DataScript operator
  |
  = help: to keep the rows that match a condition, use `where`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where amount > 10
which parses without errors
